  --> future_resource.ck:15:5
   |
15 |     a <- fork using sched
   |     ^
   = help: join it: a future of a resource is one too, joined exactly once (D156)

error[E0404]: this drops a resource of type `Future (Result File IoError)`
  --> future_resource.ck:20:5
   |
20 |     _ <- fork using sched
   |     ^ a resource must be used exactly once
   = help: bind it to a name, then join it: a future of a resource is one too (D156)

error[E0401]: `a` holds a resource (`Future (Result File IoError)`), so it must be used exactly once, but `twice` may use it more than once
  --> future_resource.ck:25:5
   |
25 |     a <- fork using sched
   |     ^
   = help: join it once: a future of a resource is one too, joined exactly once (D156)

error[E0405]: `f` holds a resource (`Future File`), which can't be put in a cown
  --> future_resource.ck:33:12
   |
33 | fn in_cown f s -> c : f~Future File, s~Sched, c~Cown (Future File)
   |            ^
   = note: `f` is passed to `cown.new`; a cown's handle can be shared, so nothing would make sure what it holds is closed (D156)
   = help: keep the resource with one owner, passing it on through calls, `fork` and `join`; a cown may hold the rest of the state

